Limit: no consumer delivers an owner-reply item yet: a completed turn's reply is durably owed and readable through pendingOwnerReplies, and delivery belongs to the U6 surface path once Hermes carries signed canonical replies (hermes-agent#63)
Limit: a Telegram ingress row keeps no chat id in the clear (payload is {text, messageId}, audit stores conversation as [not-stored]), so a Telegram reply item is addressed by the ingress claim's scope and chat digests and the owner's message id, and a sender must resolve the chat against its allowlist
Ruled-out: a dedicated owner-reply table behind a schema migration | a foreign key to canonical_turns cannot hold for the ingress lane's turn ids, and a schema bump edits the digest-pinned migrations.ts and needs an approved live migration
Ruled-out: an owner-reply kind in the governed outbox table | its rows are fenced to a role's session and swept by expiry, fencing and the generic delivery loop, none of which an owner reply may pass through before a consumer exists
Warn: the canonical sweep queues a reply only in the transaction that moves the turn to COMPLETED; queueing on every accepted COMPLETED receipt would answer a turn that a redelivery or another settlement already completed a second time
Warn: one reply per owner message is enforced by the anchor check in enqueueOwnerReply, not by the row key, because the canonical and ingress lanes mint different turn ids for the same message
Warn: an ingress claim settled by a COMPLETED receipt carries settledAt with settlement REPLY_OUTBOX and never repliedAt or noReplyAt; readers that treat settledAt as terminal rely on that
