Limit: r-1036ownerreply's Limit that a Telegram reply item is addressed by the claim's scope and chat digests, and its Warn that one reply per owner message rests on an anchor check, were true when written and are false after this commit: the address comes from the admitted payload and coverage spans every source of the turn
Ruled-out: addressing a Telegram reply from the claim's sessionDigest or legacySessionDigest | legacySessionDigest is not frozen by the identity trigger so a later write moves the reply, freezing it needs a trigger change and a migration, and a digest names a conversation without saying where it is
Ruled-out: keeping the earlier ruling against putting the Telegram chat id in the admitted payload | it leaves a Telegram reply with no immutable address; the payload-digest cost at an upgrade is accepted instead and is bounded to messages admitted before it and still unclaimed
Warn: only the turn coordinator holds a database's owner-reply authority (claimed once per database identity, released on close); anything else that needs an owner reply must go through the coordinator
Warn: reconcileIngressReceipt takes (source, query, settle) and completeClaimFromHermesReceipt accepts only a coordinator-issued, single-use IngressReceiptSettlement; code that handed the guard a receipt it built must route through the coordinator's receipt port
Warn: one owner message gets at most one reply across both lanes: a message answered through ingress (repliedAt or a reserved CEO answer) or named by another item owes nothing new, and a turn whose messages are only partly covered is refused and stays IN_DOUBT
